# ADR triggers (`rust-device-adr`)

Write an **Accepted ADR** in the consumer repo before (or with) implementation
when any of the following hold:

| Trigger | Examples |
|---------|----------|
| New platform backend split | Separate Orin vs A-box crates beyond feature flags |
| IPC encoding / capability catalog | Framing, schema versioning |
| Cloud session ownership / topology | Sole gateway vs shared; auth mechanism with expiry |
| Credential storage degradation | File-backed secrets without SE/TPM |
| Second DI mechanism | Competing containers in one binary |
| OS image / boot path | Scope beyond long-lived userspace daemon |

## Template

Use the consumer ADR template (title, status, context, decision, consequences).
Do not put product schema catalogs into this rules package.

